{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00473",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.58,
      "end_seconds": 4.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, I couldn't find the door at first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.1,
      "end_seconds": 8.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.88,
      "end_seconds": 12.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.53,
      "end_seconds": 15.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.54,
      "end_seconds": 22.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "It's cramping pain in the lower tummy. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.81,
      "end_seconds": 28.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "How long has this been going on? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.69,
      "end_seconds": 37.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Right, um, it's been going on for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.96,
      "end_seconds": 40.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What makes it worse, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.76,
      "end_seconds": 44.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I notice it more with stress and certain foods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.03,
      "end_seconds": 47.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Alright, does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.12,
      "end_seconds": 55.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.34,
      "text": "Bloating goes along with it, most of the time. Right, the bloating? That's been for four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.2,
      "end_seconds": 58.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "How much is it bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.6,
      "end_seconds": 62.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Maybe a six out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.38,
      "end_seconds": 66.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Have you been passing a lot of wind?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.91,
      "end_seconds": 87.51,
      "duration_seconds": 20.6,
      "text": "Yes, for six months. About passing a lot of wind, maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. I mean, I've also had a feeling of not emptying fully, for about a month. With feeling of not emptying fully, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.07,
      "end_seconds": 92.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Any weight loss, night-time diarrhoea or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.44,
      "end_seconds": 99.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "No weight loss, night-time diarrhoea or blood in the stool, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.37,
      "end_seconds": 102.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Alright, and fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.17,
      "end_seconds": 106.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 108.1,
      "end_seconds": 111.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.06,
      "end_seconds": 118.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.39,
      "end_seconds": 126.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Any family history of bowel cancer or anaemia at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.84,
      "end_seconds": 131.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "No, no family history of bowel cancer or anaemia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.81,
      "end_seconds": 135.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.92,
      "end_seconds": 138.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.47,
      "end_seconds": 142.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.56,
      "end_seconds": 147.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 148.8,
      "end_seconds": 156.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.35,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the escitalopram was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.35,
      "end_seconds": 161.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.88,
      "end_seconds": 168.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.41,
      "end_seconds": 172.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.75,
      "end_seconds": 177.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "About a year now. Colospa. I take it when it cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.64,
      "end_seconds": 185.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? I'll explain everything as we go along."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.19,
      "end_seconds": 187.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.88,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.77,
      "end_seconds": 188.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.47,
      "end_seconds": 190.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.13,
      "end_seconds": 199.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.15,
      "text": "I see. Okay, acid reflux, that's already on your record. Good to know. Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.63,
      "end_seconds": 201.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.98,
      "end_seconds": 205.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.24,
      "end_seconds": 209.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Of course, you know, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.66,
      "end_seconds": 227.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.76,
      "end_seconds": 231.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.39,
      "end_seconds": 233.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.53,
      "end_seconds": 237.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "No, I don't smoke and never have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.52,
      "end_seconds": 240.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Right, have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.81,
      "end_seconds": 245.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Yes, I had my appendix out, about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.12,
      "end_seconds": 249.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.59,
      "end_seconds": 260.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.23,
      "end_seconds": 283.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 98 percent, respiratory rate 16, blood pressure 112 over 81. And heart rate 65."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.59,
      "end_seconds": 284.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.24,
      "end_seconds": 289.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Right, we'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.67,
      "end_seconds": 294.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.17,
      "end_seconds": 298.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.74,
      "end_seconds": 319.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Soft tummy, a bit tender on the left lower side, no masses."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.58,
      "end_seconds": 321.28,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.73,
      "end_seconds": 349.45,
      "duration_seconds": 22.72,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out coeliac disease yet. We should do a coeliac test for bloating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.28,
      "end_seconds": 351.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.19,
      "end_seconds": 377.68,
      "duration_seconds": 25.49,
      "text": "Let's get a stool calprotectin, for bowel symptoms. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Regular meals and a bit more fibre, and don't rush your toilet time. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.5,
      "end_seconds": 393.33,
      "duration_seconds": 14.83,
      "text": "Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.83,
      "end_seconds": 395.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.64,
      "end_seconds": 404.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently. Let's review you after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.43,
      "end_seconds": 408.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.57,
      "end_seconds": 417.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "We're all set. Don't leave without asking if something's unclear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.89,
      "end_seconds": 421.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "That's everything I wanted to ask. Thank you."
    }
  ]
}